IMPORT prelude

-- Good Shepherd Nuns Ordinance 1958 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "Reverend Mother Superior of the Good Shepherd Nuns in Malaya"
-- is (s 2(1)), what a Gazette notification proves (s 4), what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do (s 2(2), (3)), how its deeds
-- are validly sealed and signed (s 3), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GSNO1958.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment
-- annotation in the body is "[7/97]" under s 5; the Legislative History names Act 7 of 1997 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act
-- 1997, in force 1 October 1997). The Ordinance is No. 45 of 1958, commenced 21 November 1958. Section numbers follow the body (s 1
-- short title to s 5 saving); the arrangement at the top of the deposit is shifted by one line by the PDF extraction.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0235 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance (historical, private and spent Acts). It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no
-- scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The Ordinance is five sections long, so the whole of it is in scope. For a person outside
-- the Congregation it matters when buying, leasing or lending on the security of the Corporation's property (s 2(3)), and in checking
-- that a deed of the Corporation was executed by the right person (ss 2(1), 3, 4).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the recitals (790 Thomson Road, 140 Ampang Road in Kuala Lumpur, the Congregation founded at Angers
-- in 1829), which are recorded in comments only; the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 3(1)
-- refers (whether a power of attorney has been "deposited" under it is taken as a stated fact); how a Reverend Mother Superior is
-- appointed, about which the Ordinance says nothing although s 2(1) speaks of appointment "as hereinafter provided"; whether a
-- Singapore Ordinance can reach property in the Federation of Malaya; the Corporation's internal governance.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Good Shepherd Nuns Ordinance 1958 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1) and 4 -- who is the Corporation, and what the Gazette proves`

-- s 2(1): "The said Reverend Mother Mary of St. Liguori and her successors for the time being in office of the Reverend Mother Superior
-- of the Good Shepherd Nuns in Malaya, duly authorised and appointed as hereinafter provided, shall be a body corporate", called the
-- "Corporation", named "Reverend Mother Superior of the Good Shepherd Nuns in Malaya", with perpetual succession and a corporate seal.
-- s 4: "A notification in the Gazette of the appointment of any person to exercise the office of Reverend Mother Superior of the Good
-- Shepherd Nuns in Malaya shall be conclusive evidence that such person was duly authorised to exercise the said office."
--
-- Two conditions in s 2(1): "for the time being in office" and "duly authorised and appointed". Nothing after s 2(1) provides how she
-- is appointed; the only later provision touching appointment is s 4, which is a rule of evidence.
-- s 4 proves that the person "was duly authorised": it speaks in the past tense and says nothing about whether she is still in office
-- (an inference from the wording, not stated).
-- `is the office-holder on the evidence` is an inference: because the Gazette notice is "conclusive", an irregular appointment that was
-- gazetted cannot be contradicted, so a person in office whose appointment is gazetted is treated as duly authorised.
DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `is for the time being in office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is duly authorised and appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointment is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds the office that is the Corporation` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is for the time being in office`
    AND `the claimant`'s `is duly authorised and appointed`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `authorisation is conclusively proved` IF
    `the claimant`'s `appointment is notified in the Gazette`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the office-holder on the evidence` IF
        `the claimant`'s `is for the time being in office`
    AND (    `the claimant`'s `is duly authorised and appointed`
          OR `authorisation is conclusively proved` `the claimant`)

§§ `2(2) and 2(3) -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): "The said seal may from time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew as the Corporation thinks fit."
-- s 2(3): "The Corporation may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may
-- sell, convey, assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable and immovable
-- property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as the Corporation thinks fit."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". Unlike the Bishop of Singapore Ordinance 1911 s 2(3), this
-- Ordinance contains no words letting the Corporation "sue and be sued". The encoding returns FALSE for powers the Ordinance does not
-- grant; whether the general law supplies them to a body corporate is outside the text and not encoded.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `break, change or remake its corporate seal`
    `acquire, purchase or take property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `convey or assign property`
    `surrender and yield up property`
    `mortgage property`
    `demise property`
    `transfer or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue in respect of its property`
    `be sued in respect of its property`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `break, change or remake its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire, purchase or take property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `convey or assign property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `surrender and yield up property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `demise property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `transfer or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 3(1): "All deeds, documents and other instruments requiring the seal of the Corporation shall be sealed with the seal of the
-- Corporation in the presence of the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being or her attorney, duly authorised by power of attorney
-- deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, and shall also be signed by the said Reverend Mother
-- Superior for the time being, or her attorney so authorised as aforesaid."
-- s 3(2): "Such signing shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence that the said seal was duly and properly affixed and that the same
-- is the lawful seal of the Corporation."
--
-- Three things must all be true: the seal, its affixing in the presence of the Reverend Mother Superior "for the time being" or a
-- deposited attorney, and the signature of one of them. A former Mother Superior does not qualify ("for the time being"). An attorney
-- whose power was never deposited does not qualify. Witness and signer need not be the same person on the words of s 3(1) (each limb
-- says the Mother Superior "or her attorney"); that reading is encoded. The Ordinance makes no provision for a vacancy in the office.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being`
    `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `a former Reverend Mother Superior`
    `another nun of the Congregation`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Mother Superior or a deposited attorney` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 3 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Mother Superior or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `is the Mother Superior or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Mother Superior or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `5 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 5: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government, all bodies politic and corporate, and all others, except
-- such as are expressly mentioned in this Ordinance and those claiming by, from or under them."
GIVEN `is expressly mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is expressly mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
